    <div class="kpi-label">Median Update Lag</div>
    <div class="kpi-sub">~3 min; 80.4% within 1 hr</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-value">7,373</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Unique Stations</div>
    <div class="kpi-sub">6 fuel types covered</div>
  </div>
</div>


<!-- ============================================================ SECTION 1: OVERVIEW -->
<section>
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-num">Section 01</div>
    <h2>Dataset Overview &amp; Coverage Summary</h2>
    <p>Scope, completeness, and temporal coverage of the analysed dataset</p>
  </div>

  <div class="two-col">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Dataset Scope</h3>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Total price observations</td><td><strong>50,000</strong></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Unique forecourts (node_ids)</td><td><strong>7,373</strong></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Fuel types present</td><td><strong>6</strong></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Earliest <em>recorded_at</em></td><td>7 Feb 2026</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Latest <em>recorded_at</em></td><td>16 Apr 2026</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Earliest <em>source_updated_at</em></td><td>17 Dec 2025</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Missing values</td><td><strong>0</strong> (all columns complete)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Rows excluded (outliers)</td><td>127 (&lt;0.3%)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="footnote">&#9432; 127 records with price_pence &lt;100p or &gt;300p excluded from distribution analysis as data-entry errors. All other statistics use the cleaned 49,873-record dataset.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h3>Records by Fuel Type</h3>
      <!-- Horizontal bar chart -->
      <div style="margin-top:4px;">
        <div class="bar-row">
          <span class="bar-label">B7_STANDARD</span>
          <div class="bar-track">
            <div class="bar-fill" style="width:89.1%; background:#7c3aed;">
              <span class="bar-val">17,818</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <span class="bar-val-outside">35.7%</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bar-row">
          <span class="bar-label">E10</span>
          <div class="bar-track">
            <div class="bar-fill" style="width:75.2%; background:#2563eb;">
              <span class="bar-val">15,044</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <span class="bar-val-outside">30.2%</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bar-row">
          <span class="bar-label">E5</span>
          <div class="bar-track">
            <div class="bar-fill" style="width:46.5%; background:#059669;">
              <span class="bar-val">9,308</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <span class="bar-val-outside">18.7%</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bar-row">
          <span class="bar-label">B7_PREMIUM</span>
          <div class="bar-track">
            <div class="bar-fill" style="width:37.8%; background:#dc2626;">
              <span class="bar-val">7,560</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <span class="bar-val-outside">15.2%</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bar-row">
          <span class="bar-label">HVO</span>
          <div class="bar-track">
            <div class="bar-fill" style="width:0.44%; background:#d97706;">
              <span class="bar-val" style="display:none;"></span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <span class="bar-val-outside">89 obs.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bar-row">
          <span class="bar-label">B10</span>
          <div class="bar-track">
            <div class="bar-fill" style="width:0.27%; background:#6b7280;">
            </div>
          </div>
          <span class="bar-val-outside">54 obs.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="footnote">B7_STANDARD and E10 together account for 65.9% of observations, reflecting their dominance at UK pumps. HVO and B10 are niche alternatives with thin data coverage.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="alert alert-info">
    <span class="alert-icon">&#8505;</span>
    <div>The dataset covers an <strong>approximately 10-week window</strong> (7 Feb–16 Apr 2026), spanning early-to-mid Q1 2026. The source brief describes the full upstream dataset as containing 396,502 rows; this sample of 50,000 rows represents ~12.6% of total coverage. All statistics and findings in this report are derived solely from this sample.</div>
  </div>
</section>


<!-- ============================================================ SECTION 2: PRICE DISTRIBUTION -->
<section>
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-num">Section 02</div>
    <h2>Price Distribution by Fuel Type</h2>
    <p>Statistical summary and visual distribution of prices across all six fuel types</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Summary Stats Table -->
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Descriptive Statistics — Price per Litre (pence), Cleaned Dataset</h3>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Fuel Type</th>
          <th>Observations</th>
          <th>Mean (p)</th>
          <th>Median (p)</th>
